take=[('Brain organization.','Brain mass, regional volume and neuron number are different measurements; most counted elephant neurons are cerebellar.'),('Sensory and motor maps.','Trigeminal trunk maps and facial motor subdivisions are specialized anatomical proposals, not complete functional circuit maps.'),('Low-frequency hearing.','A trained Asian elephant detected 16 Hz at 65 dB SPL and localized brief broadband sources around one degree.'),('Candidate seismic routes.','Foot Pacinian corpuscles and bone conduction supply anatomical and mechanical support, but their necessity for seismic behavior remains untested.'),('Controlled playback.','Ground-delivered alarm and noise stimuli change behavior; microphone controls are essential for excluding airborne leakage.'),('Discrimination and inference.','Different call and noise responses do not by themselves isolate caller recognition, threat meaning or a specific neural computation.')]
